        The root cause of the bug was related to performance issues arising from the original implementation of the "distinct from" operator, which required extracting values from blocks before performing comparisons. This extraction process introduced unnecessary overhead, leading to degraded performance, especially when dealing with large datasets. The new implementation using block/position convention allows for direct comparisons within blocks, eliminating the need for value extraction and thus improving performance.

